# Regenerated after all packet Markdown files were final, following the
# independent claude-fable-5-1 review (verdict REVISION_REQUIRED), the
# claude-fable-5-1 closure review (verdict PASS_WITH_ADVISORIES, finding F-07),
# and the corrections recorded in REVIEW_ADJUDICATION.md.
# SHA-256 of raw working-tree bytes (LF line endings). The scientific source
# baseline reviewed was commit fad5564044f6d368029bcf153fd879ec04f97fe4; the
# commit that contains this packet is necessarily later than this file and is
# determined from Git history or filled in by the reviewer.
# Paths are relative to this file.
# Verify:  Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 <file>
#     or:  sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256   (after removing these comment lines)
# This file covers every Markdown file in this directory (7 of 7) and does not
# hash itself. Its own SHA-256 is a reviewer-filled field in
# REVIEWER_DECISION_FORM.md section 5.1, which explains why no author-supplied
# value for it can exist.
# The directory also contains .gitattributes, which pins LF line endings so these
# raw-byte hashes survive a checkout on Windows (core.autocrlf=true). It is not
# hashed here: this manifest's contract covers every Markdown file and nothing
# else. The directory therefore holds nine files, seven of them Markdown.
# SHA-256 values for every source document read are in README.md section 5.
# Regenerated on owner instruction after README.md section 5 re-recorded the
# three values affected by pinning eol=lf on the parent directory. README.md
# only; the other six Markdown files are unchanged.
